WEBVTT

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.730
30-15.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.990
<i>I thought so!</i>

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.890
<i>He did that because he didn't know what to do!</i>

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.880
<i>I have the advantage on my serve!</i>

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.210
<i>I can do this! Make the next serve fast!</i>

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.000
Stop right there.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.990
Let's call this match here.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:20.740
What?!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.310
U-Um, how can you say that now?

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.630
Sorry, but I want you to call it off...
rather, put it on hold.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.720
Why?!

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.780
If you keep this up, I'm afraid 
you're going to hurt yourself.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.580
Huh?

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.850
What do you mean, you're afraid 
I'm going to hurt myself?

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.530
Nothing hurts or anything!

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.360
Well, that's because you're not injured anywhere.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.730
Please explain!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.000
What am I supposed to do 
with all this motivation?!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.870
Okay, okay, I'll explain it.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.930
I didn't think it would turn out like this, either.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.870
So, I'm sorry about that.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.460
What I wanted you to learn from this
match is the necessity of a fast serve.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.350
But I didn't realize your knowledge of 
how to move had progressed this much.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.010
It's my fault for misjudging 
your ability to analyze.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.470
I apologize.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.450
Don't let yourself get too cold.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:48.890
Right...

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.410
For someone like you to pull off a fast serve,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.390
you need the body for it, 
along with the knowledge.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.080
So what are you saying would've happened

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.400
if we'd continued that match?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:04.280
You would've undoubtedly injured either 
your lower back, shoulder, elbow, or wrist.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.040
<i>Those are all the areas I was focusing on.</i>

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.330
How can you say that with such certainty?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.280
I'm painfully aware of a 
tennis athlete's physique.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.720
When I was an active player, 
I continued playing with an injury.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:22.090
In the end, that's the reason I retired.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.430
<i>I-I had no idea...</i>

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.730
I'm going to be blunt.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.200
You can't beat Takuma yet.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.740
But I discovered something.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.210
Your body is average for a tennis player,

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.440
but it's capable of hitting a fast serve.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.450
Depending on how you execute it, 
your serve will continue to evolve.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.450
R-Really?!

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.850
Why would I lie?

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:50.230
So, starting tomorrow, why don't we work on
your serve until it's ready to conquer Japan?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.210
Yeah!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:55.210
<i>I can become stronger!</i>

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.220
First Encounter by Scouting

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.010
Pathetic.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.860
Don't cry out like that.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.480
But it really hurts!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.690
A-Anyway, you said we were 
going to practice my serve,

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.350
and all we've done is stretch.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.440
You figured it out when 
you played Takuma, right?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.120
For someone of your physique 
to hit a fast serve,

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.200
you have to loosen up your joints 
and move your body like a whip.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.460
I... u-understand, but...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.490
Good! You're joints are looking 
great from all the stretching.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.460
Ready to go on to the next step?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.120
We'll start with the overhead press.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.720
Overhead press?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.890
Yeah. It primarily enhances muscles
from the upper arms to the shoulders.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.720
Okay...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.970
Try it.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.120
Take two full seconds to push up,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.440
and four seconds to lower...

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.420
Good, you're doing exactly 
as the instructions say.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:02.450
Yeah.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:06.990
Now let's try some practical muscle 
training to help your serve.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.310
Practical?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.680
Okay, now push all the way up in one motion!

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.990
What... One motion?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.410
Too slow!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.810
Faster!

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.860
Once you raise it up, hold it for a beat.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:20.190
Then you can relax your muscles.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.000
What?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.210
If I relax now, it'll fall!

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.490
It's okay.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:25.890
I'm holding it.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.090
Now bring it down.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.770
Um, what is this exercise for?

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:38.890
You develop different muscles depending 
on whether you lift quickly or slowly.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.270
Which do you think is necessary for serving?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.400
The muscles that lift faster?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:45.580
Right.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.230
So lift it quickly!

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.180
Another thing: you develop different muscles

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:52.630
depending on whether you 
push up or lower down.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.040
Which one do you need?

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.170
The ones you get from pushing up?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:57.960
That's right!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.020
So I'll do the lowering.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:04.320
What happens if you overdevelop 
the unnecessary muscles

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:07.050
around your shoulders by lowering the weights?

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.550
<i>Overdevelop?</i>

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.410
Not like that!

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.920
Unnecessary muscles get in 
the way of bending your joints.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.060
If that happens, no matter how much 
you stretch, it won't help, right?

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:24.600
So what's important is to build only the 
necessary muscles in the necessary areas.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.910
At the same time, you also need to 
stretch to keep your joints limber,

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:32.150
so your muscles have a better range of motion, 
letting them move more easily.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.580
This allows your whip motion to 
make contact over a greater range.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.830
Okay.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.650
<i>I made up for the natural 
lack of power and strength</i>

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.370
<i>in my stroke using control.</i>

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.370
<i>I can make up for it in my serve through 
training and learning how to use my muscles.</i>

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:50.280
<i>Two months remain until the prefectural 
qualifier for the All-Japan Junior.</i>

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.760
breakfast                     tennis                              lunch
breakfast, study         opening ceremony         lunch
breakfast                     tennis                              lunch
tennis                            school
lunch
lunch

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.700
<i>And the third school term starts tomorrow.</i>

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.760
<i>I'll have to adjust my schedule.</i>

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.730
Happy New Year!

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:56.580
You, too!

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.770
Hey!

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.020
Hey, welcome back from Florida!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.530
It's been a while.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.900
How was it over there?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.240
Good. I learned a lot—

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.070
Before that, where are our souvenirs?

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.030
I brought you one.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.400
Here.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.560
Oh, a keychain? Thanks!

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.600
This one's for you, if you'd like one.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.410
Huh? Th-Thanks!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.100
Looks like we got matching ones.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.420
Huh?! Y-You're right...

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.480
You'll all start your third year this spring,

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.420
so start thinking about your future plans.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.420
<i>Future plans...</i>

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:36.070
If I can't win the All-Japan Junior,

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.770
I'll start focusing entirely on 
applying for college next summer.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:45.980
So please let me spend the next 
year focusing only on tennis!

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.070
<i>For better or for worse, 
I only have until summer.</i>

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.920
<i>I have no choice but to give it my all!</i>

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.910
We're live from the All-Japan 
Junior Indoor Invitational.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.780
Thirty-two young men and women 
have advanced through regionals

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.040
to compete in this tournament

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.300
for the title of best in Japan.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.720
Araya has improved quite a bit since last year!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.190
As expected from Okada,

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:21.640
considering he defeated Araya 
in the Kanto qualifier!

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:26.010
You take notes even during a match
between losers in the qualifiers.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:27.650
You must really love this.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.860
As time passes, the details of my notes change.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.740
What I'm doing has changed, too.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.320
That's true.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.920
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:40.510
<i>If I can learn to hit a fast serve...</i>

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:43.190
<i>As long as I'm not hit with counters 
like his in my return game,</i>

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.000
<i>I can use a wider range of attacks.</i>

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:49.600
<i>Then I can take risks in my return 
game, like Takuma-san does.</i>

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.550
<i>I have to simulate the pattern 
the best I can while I have time!</i>

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.200
Oh? If it isn't Aoi-kun!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:56.800
Hmm?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.260
Oh, Miyamoto-san, it's been a while.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.810
Yeah, since you retired.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.180
That's, what, two years?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.860
That's right.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.850
What are you up to nowadays?

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.850
I went back to STC to coach.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:11.620
Oh, let me introduce you.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:14.970
This is my first student, Maruo.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:18.120
This is Miyamoto-san from <i>Tennis Times</i>.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.570
Nice to meet you.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:20.700
Hello.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:24.960
<i>Oh. I remember him from 
last year's All-Japan Junior...</i>

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.080
I can't even imagine you being a coach!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.100
Oh, come on, Miyamoto-san.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.340
<i>It's Nabae-kun!</i>

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.850
Looks like the fan favorite has appeared.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.890
<i>I guess he really is famous.</i>

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.110
<i>It was like the whole arena 
shook for a moment.</i>

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.540
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.360
Long time no see, Nabae-kun.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.110
Sorry to make you do this 
right before your match.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.800
Hello, Miyamoto-san.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.240
It's no problem.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.590
Then let's get to it.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:04.880
This tournament has a lot of significance, 
since you're the defending

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.650
All-Japan Junior champion.

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.800
I'd like to know how you feel going into it.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:11.910
As always, I'm just going to do everything I can.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:15.190
You sound so composed!

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:17.920
Does this mean you're considering going pro?

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:23.060
If I can play the way I aspire to, 
I'm sure I'll eventually go that route.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:27.930
<i>Does that mean you can become 
a pro by mastering All-A tennis?</i>

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.360
Rather than aiming to go pro, 
Nabae simply accomplishes his goals,

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.320
and going pro is something 
that happens along the way.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.500
His battle with himself is at a higher 
level than his battle with others,

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.570
so his only option is to go pro.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:45.840
He's completely different from someone 
like you who's fighting hard to go pro.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:46.830
Yeah.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.060
<i>But...</i>

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.790
<i>I'll eventually have to defeat him,</i>

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.790
<i>or I'll never become a pro!</i>

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.700
Idiot!

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.090
What's the use in panicking now?

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:04.800
No one here is thinking of you as 
the opponent they need to beat.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.890
I-I know that much!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:08.890
Not yet, anyway.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.900
But soon enough.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.380
We're going to blow past 
everyone here soon enough!

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.400
Right!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:22.410
Outgoing Mail
Sorry to bother you while you're scouting!
I want to see you. 
Would you mind coming to the main office?
It'll take only a moment.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:24.680
There.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.910
That'll do.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:29.360
Coach!

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.880
I'm going to go buy a drink.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.170
All right. The match starts soon, so be quick.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:36.920
Okay!

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.920
Jeez, what is she up to?

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.260
<i>"I want to see you. Would you 
mind coming to the main office?"</i>

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.930
<i>I wonder what's going on with Nat-chan?</i>

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.460
U-Um... I'm going to the main office for a bit.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.440
All right.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.310
<i>How can she say things like 
"I want to see you" so easily?</i>

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:00.440
<i>Is she just not thinking about it, or what?</i>

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.450
Huh? Which way's the main office, again?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:08.650
I-I'm sorry!

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.500
No, I'm sorry...

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.000
<i>A cell phone battery?</i>

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.520
Oh... It went off...

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.510
Huh?!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:31.130
There's a huge dent in it!

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.410
Excuse me...

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.520
You dropped this.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.170
Oh, okay...

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:39.020
And that's not a dent.

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.460
Put this in, and...

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:45.740
put the cover on.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:46.530
There.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:50.020
Um... The screen is still black.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:51.710
Try turning the power on.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.540
Huh?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.540
It turned on!

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:02.420
I-I'm sorry. I'm really bad with cell phones.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.550
<i>That's pretty rare nowadays.</i>

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:07.250
Um, thank you very much.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:10.360
I wanted to contact my mother, 
so you really helped me out.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.430
No problem.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:14.150
<i>She's a bit odd.</i>

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:15.740
Oh, Ei-chan!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.710
Nat-chan!

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.440
I was just making my way over to you.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.530
Oh, it's Shimizu-san!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.430
Hi there!

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.180
H-Hello.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.030
You know her, Nat-chan?

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.240
Yeah, you're Shimizu Aki-chan, right?

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.590
Of course I know her.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:35.040
She's the girls' first seed.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.290
What?! F-First seed?!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.270
<i>You're kidding me, right?!</i>

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.810
Um, sorry for causing you trouble.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:43.550
I'll be going now.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.300
Thank you for your help.

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:49.990
You really haven't heard of Shimizu-san?

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:50.740
Nope.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.700
I don't know anything about the girls.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:55.060
But that must mean she's really good, right?

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.730
She's super good!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:01.320
She won last year's All-Japan 
Junior as a first-year!

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.070
What?!

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.460
She's been training with 
her mom, who's her coach,

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.460
and aiming to go pro since she was young.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:09.820
So she's always been good.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.820
I've been up against her 
four times in three years,

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:15.830
but never won.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.330
<i>What?! Nat-chan lost all four matches?!</i>

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:22.030
But lately, I feel like I've 
caught up to her a little!

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:25.270
So if I win my way up here, 
I'll face her in the semifinals.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.550
I want to get to that point.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:30.550
And... I want to beat her just 
once before I go pro, if I can.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.620
<i>I never knew...</i>

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:36.560
<i>Nat-chan had someone she wanted to 
beat the way I want to beat Nabae-kun.</i>

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:40.500
By the way, were you and Shimizu-san 
talking about something?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.160
Oh, yeah.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.570
I just put her cell phone battery back in for her.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:48.900
I see. She is cute, after all, isn't she?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.820
That has nothing to do with anything.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.710
But more importantly, you messaged me, right?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.720
What's up?

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.330
Oh, that's right.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.460
I know you're busy, but...

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:03.840
I was wondering if you could come 
watch my match for just a bit...

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.250
Sure, I'll be over there by the second round.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.340
What?!

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.160
That won't work.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.540
Just come for the very 
beginning, just for a bit...

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.850
Just a game or two is enough, so please!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:19.010
<i>I get it... She still gets nervous 
during the first round.</i>

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:20.350
Okay, I'll go.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.800
Yay! Thank you!

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.700
But there are a lot of matches I need to watch,

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.020
so I really may be there only for the first game.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.290
That's fine.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.490
I'm just nervous at the start.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.620
You're the only one who 
understands stuff like this...

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:37.310
Just having you there will calm me down.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.870
So I'll be fine now!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.210
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.200
<i>She really believes she'll be fine now.</i>

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.380
All right!

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:45.850
I'll be going now!

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:55.930
Love-15.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:57.180
Yes!

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.240
<i>Yes!</i>

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.610
<i>Looks like she's up to the challenge.</i>

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.190
That's it, Aki!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.510
That was good!

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.940
Keep it up on the next one!

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:07.940
<i>Aki... As in...</i>

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.320
<i>That's Shimizu-san from earlier!</i>

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.950
<i>Which means that must be her mom?</i>

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:15.450
<i>Wow, that's incredible.</i>

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.330
<i>All her moves are efficient...</i>

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.950
<i>And quick, and accurate.</i>

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.200
<i>She's like a machine.</i>

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:26.210
<i>So this is the wall that Nat-chan 
wants to make it over, just like mine.</i>

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.300
<i>You can do it, Nat-chan!</i>

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.960
<i>I'm gonna do my best, too!</i>

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.150
Ugh, it's cold!

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:08.290
Therefore, if you move <i>k</i> along the 
<i>y</i>-axis in a parallel manner...

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.900
<i>So sleepy...</i>

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:07.710
<i>Second period is when I always feel 
my first wave of sleepiness.</i>

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.570
<i>No, that's no good!</i>

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:13.300
<i>I don't have time to study at home, 
so I have to pay attention now!</i>

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.720
All right, that's all for today.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.150
Oh, boy.

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.770
His switch completely turns 
off after class ends.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:27.650
Even during breaks, Ei-chan's 
only awake to eat lunch.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:30.440
He says he's tired from training so hard lately.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.200
Hey, Kageyama-kun...

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.200
Is it true that Maruo-kun can't 
go on the class field trip?

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.400
Yeah, Nat-chan can't, either.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:40.880
What?! Why?!

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.800
Apparently, it's really bad 
for them to stop training

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:45.960
for three or four days before a match.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.990
Their world is so different.

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:50.600
If they're going through all that,
I sure hope they win.

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.860
But it really is a pity!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.280
<i>My four-day trip with Maruo-kun...</i>

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:55.280
<i>My four-day trip with Takasaki-san...</i>

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.970
<i>What the heck were you expecting?</i>

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.720
Whew, it's finally over.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:02.900
Hey, Maruo-kun!

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.970
Do you have a second?

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:09.100
It's about the future plans form you turned in.

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.450
You wrote "tennis player,"

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.230
and I wanted to know how 
serious you were about that.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.370
Right.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:18.550
I plan to continue that path 
until August of my third year,

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.660
and my parents agreed to it.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.290
I see.

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:25.650
I knew you weren't the type to joke 
around about matters like that, but...

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:27.400
With grades like yours,

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:31.700
if you study hard, you can still aim to get 
into a top university by recommendation.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:36.280
Did you make your decision knowing that 
August is the cutoff for a recommendation?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.170
Yes.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.800
If I don't win the All-Japan Junior in August,

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.170
I'll give up on tennis.

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:46.400
Well, I'll talk to you later.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:47.680
Let's talk in detail next time.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:51.930
Hey, Ei-chan.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:53.770
Huh? He's not here?

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.070
You need Ei-chan for something?

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:59.270
I came to borrow the Ei-chan Notes for 
world history. But he's not here, huh?

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.030
What the hell? He's so useless.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.930
Ei-chan's pretty busy lately.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.290
Tennis again?

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.950
He has a big tournament coming up.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.430
A tournament, huh?

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:10.720
I heard a rumor.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.180
He suddenly started saying 
he wants to go pro, right?

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:14.840
Is he confused or something?

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:16.290
It's hilarious!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.050
Takuma-senpai is one thing, 
but there's no way <i>he</i> can go pro.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.670
Well, I didn't have much hope for him, either,

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:25.930
but after playing for two years, 
he's starting to show a lot of promise.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.270
Huh? Yeah, but we're talking about going pro!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.560
That's impossible!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:33.920
If he has time to daydream, he should 
be taking useful notes, like he used to.

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:38.110
Yeah, really. His notes are 
missing a lot of details lately.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.020
Trying to go pro? Is he seriously stupid?

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:44.120
Well, it's impossible anyway!

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:45.620
What's your problem?!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.630
What do you mean by that?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.360
You have no right to ridicule
Ei-chan when you're the ones

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.760
borrowing notes to get out of studying for tests!

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:55.630
And you'd better stop talking 
about Ei-chan like that.

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:58.340
You have no idea how much 
effort he's putting in!

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.730
Are you in any place to talk?

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:03.210
You're always depending on Ei-chan.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.050
Lame.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.380
You can say whatever you want about me!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:10.430
But if you keep making fun of 
Ei-chan, I won't let you off easy!

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.180
Let's go.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.400
Y-Yeah.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.800
Kageyama? Whats going on?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.430
Nothing, really.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:25.990
Done talking to the teacher?

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.160
Yeah.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:31.860
I'm not sure he understands, but it's 
something I just have to work hard at.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.250
I guess.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.250
Oh?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.950
You get a second wave of 
sleepiness in the afternoon?

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:42.890
Yeah, a really intense one.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:46.480
I'm always fighting to stay awake during class.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:48.290
Keep at it, Ei-chan!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:48.760
Yeah.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.770
Oh, it's snowing!

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.810
Damn, it's snowing?

00:20:58.680 --> 00:20:59.770
Well, can't help that.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.480
Guess I'm weight training indoors today.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:04.680
Koshimizu, are you on your way to practice?

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.040
Huh? Yeah...

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:10.130
Maruo, are you planning on going pro?

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:10.770
Huh?

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:13.370
Well, yeah. I plan on it.

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:14.650
What about you?

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:19.130
Idiot. You and I are on 
totally different levels.

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:21.130
Good luck.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.380
Yeah. Thanks.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.390
Snowing, snowing!

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:34.890
Oh, yeah, Nat-chan. I heard you made 
the top four for the All-Japan Junior!

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:36.570
Oh, yeah.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.800
That's your personal best! Congratulations!

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:39.900
Thanks.

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:43.900
But I lost to Shimizu-san again.

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.400
Shimizu-san? That girl from...

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.640
This one was the most frustrating yet.

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.410
I was so close...

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.420
Then let's win the All-Japan Junior!

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:05.720
And let's both win and go pro together!

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:11.230
Uh... I can't talk that big for myself yet, but...

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:14.390
I meant, let's use that same determination

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.430
to motivate us in the tournament...

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:19.940
<i>Oh, no. I'm starting to 
feel really embarrassed!</i>

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:21.910
Yeah!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:03.000
For me, this will be the 
challenge of a lifetime.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.430
The Kanagawa Junior Tennis
Tournament is about to begin.

00:24:05.430 --> 00:24:08.430
Nat-chan always tells me 
to try my best, but...

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:10.050
Today she said, "Let's do our best."

00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:14.090
She considers me someone she can 
aim for the nationals with because

00:24:14.090 --> 00:24:16.010
she knows how much I've done to get here.

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:18.010
If I lose, I'll have to give up on going pro.

00:24:18.270 --> 00:24:20.890
I just have to believe in myself and fight!

00:24:20.890 --> 00:24:22.600
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Revenge at the Critical Moment

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.140
"Revenge at the Critical Moment."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:32.280
End
